      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could the subject and message say what this patch changes? As far as I can see, the `-EINVAL` for cross-slice `MREMAP_FIXED` moves and the slice-preserving hint search were already there (aosp/4312522). What\u0027s new is that file, shmem and private /dev/zero mappings can now move to another slice, where they got `-EINVAL` before. The last paragraph describes the alignment lines, which this patch no longer touches, so I think it can go.\n\nSomething like:\n\n```\nANDROID: P3S: mm/mremap: Let file mappings move to another slice\n\nIn a 4KB process, an MREMAP_FIXED move to another slice of a 16KB\nwindow fails with -EINVAL for every VMA. Only anonymous VMAs need\nthat: their slice follows the virtual address, and moving their PTEs\nto another slice would mean copying the pages, which would break pins\non the old folios.\n\nFile, shmem and private /dev/zero mappings map folios by offset, so\nthey can keep their slice in vm_slice_off. Check the slice in\ncheck_prep_vma(), where the VMA is known, and skip the check for\nthem. copy_vma() then gives the new VMA the slice of the source\naddress.\n```",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "80ea5f3da379dde9cbb464a26d5db7c6ec40a6ae",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
