      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the new subject. Could the body still say what fails today? As far as I can see, it explains why anonymous moves stay rejected and why file mappings could move. It doesn\u0027t say that a cross-slice `MREMAP_FIXED` gets `-EINVAL` for file mappings too, or that this is about 4KB processes. Something like this as the first paragraph:\n\n```\nIn a 4KB process, an MREMAP_FIXED move to another slice of a 16KB\nwindow fails with -EINVAL for every VMA. Only anonymous VMAs need\nthat: copying their contents to new folios would break references\nand DMA pins. File, shmem and private /dev/zero mappings retain their\nbacking offset and can move their PTEs without copying pages.\n```\n\nI think the last line, \"Keep the existing alignment and nonbinding-hint rules unchanged.\", can go, since the patch doesn\u0027t touch that code.",
